cept the ethics lawyer for president  george w bush  so you are probably okay using the term  so there's a good chance you may have  committed some light treason what should  you do now - once again paraphrase the  former NSA and Naval War College figure  John Schindler first ones to make a deal  usually get the lightest prison  sentences Friday security expert Harvard  lecturer somebody I was proud to help  bring to MSNBC Juliet km put together  three mildly interesting facts and  realized that one other name was missing  and that name and why it was missing was  way more interesting  former Trump campaign manager Paul  Manafort volunteered for a limited  interview with the House Intelligence  Committee and said he talked to the  Senate Intelligence Committee to  longtime Trump's stooge Roger stone  demanded to make an appearance before  the House Intelligence Committee  the second man every name by Trump is a  foreign policy advisor Carter page also  said he would talk to the House  Intelligence Committee Monday morning  the New York Times revealed Jared  Kushner whose best-known skill is that  he has survived being Trump's son-in-law  has been asked to testify to the Senate  Intelligence Committee but is juliek I  am realized the other key actor in  whatever the Trump Russia dance of  deceit really is he hasn't said boo  about testifying anywhere General  Michael Flynn thus says Juliet the  question in the intelligence and  security circles in which she travels is  increasingly becoming could Flynn be  cutting a deal with the FBI Flynn of  course was briefly the national security  adviser until it turned out not only  that so many wild reports about him and  foreign governments were true but that  some of them were sanitized versions of  true but then it turned out he was also  on the Trump campaign team and the  Turkish payrolls simultaneously and now  the former CIA director james Woolsey  says he was at a meeting last summer at  which Flynn on the Trump campaign team  talked to Turkish officials about  returning to Turkish custody the muslim  cleric on whom the turkish dictator  erawan has blamed all his country's  problems and you can translate that  statement as kidnap a legal resident of  the United States from his home in  Pennsylvania  and then take him to imprisonment and/or  death in Turkey making a deal to flip  and tell all he knows about Trump or  whoever might be Flynn's only way out  now since he could be charged with some  traitorous offenses involving two  different foreign countries his reaction  to the story that he might have made a  deal his spokesman told a reporter Flynn  is not quote responding as Humphrey  Bogart who'd to Mary Astor in The  Maltese Falcon don't be Shelly you're  taking the fall funny that Juliet  Cayenne would wonder whether Mike Flynn  may have made a deal with the FBI scene  this blood-curdling cover of the Trump  friendly tabloid the National Enquirer  Trump catches Russia's White House spy  how he tricked the bungling FBI 23  agents have infiltrated Congress federal  bureaus in the military spoiler alert  they mean General Michael Flynn but  there are plenty of buses under which  plenty of the Trump Putin Easter's can  be successfully thrown The Associated  Press story that Paul Manafort signed a  10 million dollar contract in 2006 with  a Russian oligarch the deal Manafort  said would quote greatly benefit the  Putin government the Trump government  had already been distancing itself from  Manta Ford downplaying his efforts with  the campaign saying he was somebody who  played a very limited role for a very  limited amount of time as somebody only  there to count delegates Paul Manafort  was Donald Trump's second campaign  manager all that is missing for Paul  Manafort now is the bus and remember  what mom always said never run for the  bus there will always be another one and  lastly in American politics we have seen  guilty suspects panic and innocent  suspects panic and vindicated suspects  panic but not since ken starr have we  seen somebody who is in effect the  prosecutor panic Devan noonish chairman  of the House Intelligence Committee is  acting like a guy who is about to flee  the country he told the media he had  some kind of intelligence information  that somehow backstopped Trump's  wiretapping hoax and he possibly  violated the law just by saying that to  the  Media he then took that information to  Trump like a prosecutor handing over  evidence to a defendant or at least the  associate of a defendant possibly  violating the law again he explained he  did this amazingly stupid thing because  Trump had been quote taking a lot of  heat in the media he did this before  sharing any of whatever the Intel was  with the rest of his own committee he  had to apologize to his own committee he  then was unable or unwilling to deny  that this information that supposedly  supported Trump originated with Trump  and then The Daily Beast quoted three  unnamed committee officials and a former  national security official who said that  the night before all this started  newness was in an uber with a staffer he  got a call or a text or an email and  immediately bolted out of the car and  though he later denied going missing for  hours it seemed nobody knew where he was  and Monday morning it was reported  newness was at the White House that day  to meet his Intel source but his  spokesman said that while yes he was on  the White House grounds he didn't go to  the White House itself because this is  what happens when you elect Inspector  Clouseau to Congress this is the man  nominally leading the congressional  investigation of Trump and Russia who of  course was also a member of Trump's  presidential transition team and just  happened to be at one of general Flynn's  meetings with the Turkish Foreign  Minister and all this unfolds while my  friend Andrew Mitchell reported quote a  lot of former transition team members in  and outside of the Whi